    "category": "Indicator",
    "type_designations": ["ZM505 / ZM510 / ZM605 / ZM615 Series", "ZM505", "ZM510", "ZM605", "ZM615"],
    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Family of programmable, self-indicating, mains, DC or battery-powered indicators designed to be used as part of Class III or IIII non-automatic weighing instruments. Construction designation 'Prefix-XYZ': model prefix ZM505/ZM510/ZM605/ZM615 = standard indicator; X = enclosure material (S = stainless enclosure); Y = mounting orientation (D = desktop, P = panel mount); Z = display type (3 = IBN dot graphic, black background with green digits; 4 = dot graphic, green background with black dots, capable of negative image; 5 = large dot graphic, green backlight with black dots, capable of negative image). Devices: semi-automatic zero setting (max 4% Max), zero tracking (max 4% Max), semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, pre-set tare, recall of gross indication when tare active, determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, checking of display, printing, PLUs, alibi storage, gravity compensation, real time clock, command via external device (PC), single or multi-range/multi-interval operation (max 3 partial ranges), range in use indicators, connection to up to 4 load receptors with load receptor number indicator, and connection to digital load cells. Standard interfaces: 4-wire or 6-wire shielded load cell connection, 3 logic level inputs, 3 open collector outputs, 3 RS232 serial ports, 10/100 Ethernet, 2 USB host ports. Optional interface cards/PCBs: analogue output (0-10 VDC, 4-20 mA), current loop (4-20 mA, RS485/RS422), wireless LAN 802.11b/g, USB device, 5V or 10V excitation load cell interface boards, Bluetooth, DeviceNet, Profibus, Ethernet PoE pass-through, quad DC input/output, quad AC input/output, external I/O expansion, programmable digital I/O. Legally relevant software AWT30-500208, protected by sealed jumper or password/incrementing counters. May be connected to a maximum of two Avery Weigh-Tronix BSQ series digital bases."
  },
